## The important Helm concept

Don't think of Helm as replacing Kubernetes.

Think of it this way:

```text
             Helm
              │
              │ generates/manages
              ▼
       Kubernetes manifests
              │
              ▼
       Kubernetes API Server
              │
       ┌──────┼──────┐
       ▼      ▼      ▼
     Deploy  Service Ingress
       │
       ▼
      Pods
```

And for your particular application:

```text
                  HELM
                   │
                   ▼
             ecommerce chart
                   │
       ┌───────────┼───────────┐
       ▼           ▼           ▼
     USER        PRODUCT      ORDER
       │           │           │
       ▼           ▼           ▼
   Deployment  Deployment  Deployment
       │           │           │
       ▼           ▼           ▼
    Service     Service     Service
                               │
                    ┌──────────┴──────────┐
                    │                     │
                    ▼                     ▼
               user-service        product-service
```

**One Helm chart → one release → multiple microservices.**

For your next step, the best improvement would be to refactor this into a **generic Helm template using a `services` array**, so you don't need three separate deployment/service YAML files. That is the pattern you'll commonly see in more sophisticated multi-service deployments.



